viogpudo: the host screen's vertical blank as ours (host-vblank).

On top of 01 to 03.  When the device offers 2ksbox's host-vblank feature
(bit 23, QEMU patch 90) the driver takes it, and while dxgkrnl has the
vertical blank interrupt on it asks the device for the host's blanks
(command 0x0f00, sent from the worker thread, since the control queue
needs PASSIVE_LEVEL and DxgkDdiControlInterrupt may come higher).  Each
host blank arrives as the config interrupt with bit 31 of events_read: the
interrupt routine clears it and raises DXGK_INTERRUPT_DISPLAYONLY_VSYNC at
once, and runs the display-event path only when another event came with
it, so a tick never makes viogpuap resync the resolution.  The timer of
01 stays as the fallback: it raises the blank only when no host blank
came for two periods and a half (a minimized player window, a host that
stops), and alone on a device without the feature.  The worker thread now
runs ConfigChanged only for a display event.

